import rutile;

/*
I will use C and C++ language to explain the code.
Rutile is a programming language meant to be a replacement for C++.
It uses alot of the same components, but replaces bad defaults with better ones and tries to fix the issues that C++ has.
It is a compiled language and meant for software development.
You can assume it has the same rules as C++, unless I specify otherwise.
It is also a statically typed language, meaning that the types of variables are known at compile time.
So really, C++ but better.
*/


